    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "## Scope (Chat 03B1 / issue #439)\nIsolated, undeployed **D1-compatible SQLite atomic transition foundation** for future authoritative gameplay storage. Four new files only; no runtime, telemetry, economy, UI, NPC, voting or Stage 7.15 changes.\n\n- `gameplay-server/migrations/0001_tactical_state.sql`: distinct `gameplay_battles`, `gameplay_command_receipts`, `gameplay_event_outbox`. An `INSTEAD OF INSERT` trigger on a write-only view validates version/CAS, immutable participant snapshot fields, event IDs and writes state+receipt+outbox in **one SQL statement**. Stale version or event collision aborts the statement. This addresses the 0-row UPDATE issue in D1 `batch()`.\n- `gameplay-server/test/test_cas_sql.py`: ten real-SQLite unit/integration cases, including two-connection same-version race and rollback.\n- `.github/workflows/chat03b1-gameplay-cas.yml`: isolated PR CI for SQLite integration tests.\n- `gameplay-server/README.md`: transaction and trust-boundary contract.\n\n**IMPORTANT:** This PR is NOT an approved gameplay backend, NO production DB provisioned/deployed, NO player authentication, NO network API, NO D1 runtime test, NO secure PvP claim. It must remain Draft; actual Cloudflare D1 trigger/concurrency behavior is a later gate. It explicitly does not touch `telemetry-receiver` or its 30-day retention.\n\nBase: `main@57244500e58d1ee6f0b7f2f5e87cd2e63bb83dcb` (PR #438 merged).\nReference: [issue #439](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/issues/439), [Chat 03 Notion](https://app.notion.com/p/3fc815ae752f81968c5bf2b09c262045).\n\n**Tests:** dedicated GitHub Actions workflow added; outcomes to be checked on exact PR HEAD. Only SQLite migration smoke independently exercised before PR; no full-suite result claimed yet.\n\n**Next review:** inspect real SQLite concurrency/CAS outcome, D1 compatibility and SQL trigger security. Don't merge until independent review and architecture approval.",
